  "description": "The Flyte traces its roots to the Moulton Y-frame concept bikes of the 1970s. Once limited by market shifts and patent restrictions, it now benefits from modern materials and advanced engineering. Embodying Moulton’s vision of a high-performance, practical urban bicycle, it retains core principles - compact yet stiff construction, front and rear suspension - plus a frame with ergonomic 'carrying handle'. Lighter and more refined, the Flyte finally brings a once-unattainable concept to life!",
